##READ RULES AND SOURCE CLIPS 
Before editing or publishing anything, carefully understand the campaign requirements. 
Every clipping campaign can have different rules, payment structures and submission procedures.


Read the campaign rules - 
Read the campaign guidelines carefully ( rules documents is mostly given in campaign brief ). 
Check which social media platforms are accepted (Instagram, TikTok, YouTube Shorts, etc.).
Check the minimum and maximum video duration.
Understand the requirements for captions, subtitles and hashtags.
Check whether watermarks or specific branding are required.
Understand how views are tracked and verified.
Check the payment structure (CPM/RPM or fixed payment).
Note the campaign deadline and remaining budget.
Check prohibited content and submission requirements.


Download source clips - 
Visit the campaign's official source-material section.
Look for Google Drive folders, Dropbox links or direct video downloads.
Select suitable footage from the available source videos.
Download the original videos in the highest available quality.
Organize the downloaded videos into folders for easier editing.


Organize your source material - 
Clipping/
│
├── Campaign-Name/
│   ├── Source-Videos/
│   ├── Selected-Clips/
│   ├── Edited-Videos/
│   └── Published-Clips/


Important considerations - 
Use campaign-authorized footage.
Don't download random creators' content without permission.
Avoid copyrighted music and unauthorized third-party footage.
Keep the original source files for future editing.
Prioritize videos containing engaging conversations, controversial opinions, entertaining moments or valuable information.
